<Base title="Contact - Coldwast" description="How to reach the Coldwast editorial team: corrections, technical questions and takedown requests." path="/contact.html">
  <div class="reading">
  <p class="kicker" style="margin-top:30px">Coldwast</p>
  <h1>Contact</h1>

  <p>Coldwast is an independent publication of programming guides. If something on this site is
  wrong, out of date, or unclear, we would rather hear it than leave it standing.</p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p><a href="mailto:referencement.frb@gmail.com">referencement.frb@gmail.com</a></p>
  <p>Write in English or French. There is no form on this page and no third-party service in
  between: the address opens your own mail client, and nothing you type is sent to this site.</p>

  <h2>What is worth writing about</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Factual corrections.</strong> A command that no longer works, a flag that changed
    between toolchain versions, a link that has rotted. Include the page URL and, if you can, the
    version you tested with, it makes the fix much faster.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical questions</strong> about a guide, when the guide itself does not answer
    them. Gaps like these usually mean the guide should be improved.</li>
    <li><strong>Attribution and takedown.</strong> The domain <code>coldwa.st</code> previously
    hosted a personal Haskell blog that is gone. We publish original work under an independent
    editorial identity and never present it as that author's. If you believe something here
    infringes your rights or misattributes your work, write and we will act on it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who publishes this</h2>
  <p>Coldwast is run by an independent editorial team, not by a company acting on behalf of the
  vendors it writes about. Our editorial policy, the history of this domain and our affiliate
  disclosure are set out on the <a href="/about.html">about page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
